From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] windows.ui.xaml: application resources -- App.xaml, ResourceDictionary.Source, newer compiled dictionaries, system colours

An application's resources (its App.xaml: theme dictionaries, control styles, its own resource dictionary classes) were never loaded: NanaZip's App does not load its App.xaml itself, and ResourceDictionary.Source did nothing. App.xaml is now loaded for the application before its first markup or island content unless it loads it itself; ResourceDictionary.Source (from code or markup, ms-appx:/// or a path from the application's folder; XAML text or compiled, also a .xbf named directly) loads the dictionary, a loop of Sources failing. Compiled dictionaries as newer compilers write them are read: dictionary references of kind 10 with conditional XAML (a key's alternatives chosen by IsApiContractPresent/NotPresent predicates; every contract counts as present) and types given by XML namespace (type flag 2). The desktop's colours are offered as the system colour resources (SystemColor*Color, SystemAccentColor and its light and dark shades, UseSystemFocusVisuals, SymbolThemeFontFamily). Kind 10 and type flag 2 are not described by XbfAnalyzer; their layout is taken from observed files (NanaZip's Mile.Xaml.Styles.SunValley.xbf and App.xbf, read as data). Behind the XAML switch of 6131.
---
diff --git a/dlls/windows.ui.xaml/application.c b/dlls/windows.ui.xaml/application.c
index 519a112..5338b5a 100644
--- a/dlls/windows.ui.xaml/application.c
+++ b/dlls/windows.ui.xaml/application.c
@@ -51,6 +51,7 @@ struct application
     INT32 focus_visual_kind;
     boolean requires_pointer_mode;
     INT32 high_contrast_adjustment;
+    BOOL markup_loaded;                 /* its App.xaml */
     struct handler_list unhandled_exception, suspending, resuming, leaving_background, entered_background;
 };
 
@@ -315,6 +316,41 @@ IInspectable *xaml_application_resources( IInspectable *app_iface )
     return app->resources;
 }
 
+/* App.xaml holds the application's resources (the dictionaries its pages use).  A program whose App
+ * does not load it itself has it loaded before the first other markup or content: when XAML first
+ * needs it, as with a framework-activated application. */
+void xaml_application_load_markup(void)
+{
+    IInspectable *app;
+    BOOL load;
+    HRESULT hr;
+
+    EnterCriticalSection( &app_cs );
+    if ((load = current_app && !current_app->markup_loaded)) current_app->markup_loaded = TRUE;
+    LeaveCriticalSection( &app_cs );
+#ifdef SG_MUTANT_XAML_NO_APP_MARKUP
+    load = FALSE;
+#endif
+    if (!load || !(app = xaml_current_application())) return;
+    hr = xaml_load_uri( app, L"ms-appx:///App.xaml" );
+    if (FAILED(hr)) WARN( "App.xaml not loaded: %#lx\n", hr );
+    else TRACE( "App.xaml %s\n", hr == S_OK ? "loaded" : "not there" );
+    IInspectable_Release( app );
+}
+
+/* a component's markup is loaded: the program's own App.xaml, or other markup that may use it */
+void xaml_application_markup_loading( IInspectable *component, const WCHAR *uri )
+{
+    if (uri && !wcsicmp( uri, L"ms-appx:///App.xaml" ))
+    {
+        EnterCriticalSection( &app_cs );
+        if (current_app) current_app->markup_loaded = TRUE;
+        LeaveCriticalSection( &app_cs );
+        return;
+    }
+    xaml_application_load_markup();
+}
+
 /* the application object (its outer: the program's App), with a reference */
 IInspectable *xaml_current_application(void)
 {
